      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2010 THE AUTHORS. BJU INTERNATIONAL © 2010 BJU INTERNATIONAL.",
        "AbstractText": "\u2022 Our traditional approach to managing the chronic prostatitis (CP) syndromes has not been very successful for many of our patients. \u2022 Our developing understanding of CP/chronic pelvic pain syndrome (CP/CPPS) as a heterogeneous syndrome rather than a homogenous disease has allowed us to develop treatment strategies based on individual patient characteristics. \u2022 By considering each patient as a unique individual and tailoring treatments to a specific patient's clinical 'phenotype' we improve our therapeutic outcomes."
      },
